content.text:
This confirms baa0bf9 only touched the API key/formatting, not the setAdapter logic. So the bug was introduced in 31540ff, which removed the initial `gridview.setAdapter(imageAdapter)` call in `onCreateView` and only set it later inside the async network response's `runOnUiThread`.

## Bug-Introducing Commits
BIC: 31540ff5f39715a51ea0b7f4a7f516284d27888d

## Reasoning

**(1) Investigation:** I traced the file history with `git log -p --follow` on `MainActivityFragment.java` to find every commit touching `gridview.setAdapter`. The fix commit (550830f) simply re-adds `gridview.setAdapter(imageAdapter);` right after `gridview` is bound via `findViewById` in `onCreateView`. I searched backward for the commit that removed this line.

**(2) The introducing change:** Commit `31540ff` ("Grid image issue resolved") removed the line
```java
gridview.setAdapter(imageAdapter);
```
from `onCreateView` (where it originally ran synchronously right after the GridView was found), and moved the adapter-attachment logic into the network response's `runOnUiThread` block inside `getMovies()`:
```java
getActivity().runOnUiThread(new Runnable() {
    @Override
    public void run() {
        gridview.setAdapter(imageAdapter);
    }
});
```
This meant the GridView no longer got an adapter attached at fragment creation time — it would only get one once (and each time) a network response arrived. This is consistent with the class of bug the fix addresses: the grid could appear empty/unresponsive until the async callback fired, or in some cases never got wired up if `onCreateView`-time UI logic depended on an adapter being present immediately.

**(3) Supporting evidence:** The very next commit, `baa0bf9` ("remove API key"), only changes whitespace/the hardcoded API key/log line and does not touch the `setAdapter` logic at all — confirming it isn't the source of the bug. The bug-fix diff exactly restores the single line removed in `31540ff`, in the exact original location (immediately after `gridview = (GridView) mainFragmentView.findViewById(R.id.gridView);`), which is strong evidence that `31540ff` is where the regression was introduced.

I'm fairly confident in this attribution since the fix is a literal one-line reintroduction of code that was deleted in `31540ff` and never restored in the intervening commit.

